{%- comment -%}
  Wig Party — collection filter flash guard. Renders no visible markup; place this section
  immediately BEFORE `collection-results` (type `collection-results`, section id commonly
  `results`) in the template order so its <style> is parsed before any of that section's
  content.

  The problem: sections/collection-results.liquid renders Shopify's native filters
  (Availability, Price) and the non-theme quick chips (Everything, Under $300) visible on
  first paint, while the custom theme_filter groups/chips (Cap construction, Colour
  family, …) render with the `hidden` attribute. assets/aria-collection.js fetches every
  product (?view=aria-index) on DOMContentLoaded, counts the theme filters, then unhides
  them — about a 1s gap in which only the native/quick set is visible, so the sidebar
  visibly changes shape a second later.

  The fix only uses the `aria-coll--counting` class that collection-results.liquid's own
  inline script already adds to the section root (`document.currentScript.parentNode
  .classList.add('aria-coll--counting')`, the very first thing inside <section data-aria-
  coll>, before any sidebar/chip markup exists) and that aria-collection.js only ever
  REMOVES (`.finally(done)`, plus early-return paths) — never adds. So this class behaves
  like a server-set class for flash purposes: there is no race against the external script
  adding it late. No markup or script in collection-results.liquid, aria-collection.js, or
  any other shared file is touched; this file only adds CSS (plus a small, self-contained
  accessibility script scoped to `[data-aria-coll]`, which already exists in that server
  markup).

  While `.aria-coll--counting` is present:
    - native filter groups (`.aria-coll__group` without `data-aria-coll-theme-group`) and
      non-theme chips (`.aria-coll__chip` without `data-aria-coll-theme-chip`) are hidden
      via visibility/opacity, not display:none, so they keep reserving their real layout
      box — no extra min-height hack needed.
    - the already-`hidden` theme groups/chips/options are shown as reserved, invisible
      space too (a higher-specificity override of collection-results' own
      `.aria-coll [hidden] { display: none !important }`), so the sidebar doesn't grow
      when their real counts land a moment later; everything becomes visible together.
    - a pure-CSS `animation-delay` reveals all of it anyway after ~3s if the fetch never
      resolves or aria-collection.js errors before clearing the class — no JS timer drives
      the visual reveal.

  Works at every viewport (visibility-based, no size-specific rule needed), so there is no
  separate mobile block.

  Caveat: a theme-filter group/option that ends up with zero matching products still
  contracts (hidden attribute takes effect) once counting finishes and this CSS stops
  applying — unavoidable since the real result isn't known until the count completes.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  .aria-coll--counting .aria-coll__group:not([data-aria-coll-theme-group]),
  .aria-coll--counting .aria-coll__chip:not([data-aria-coll-theme-chip]) {
    visibility: hidden;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: wp-coll-guard-reveal 0s 3s forwards;
  }

  .aria-coll--counting [data-aria-coll-theme-group][hidden] {
    display: block !important;
    visibility: hidden;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: wp-coll-guard-reveal 0s 3s forwards;
  }

  .aria-coll--counting [data-aria-coll-theme-chip][hidden] {
    display: inline-flex !important;
    visibility: hidden;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: wp-coll-guard-reveal 0s 3s forwards;
  }

  .aria-coll--counting [data-aria-coll-theme-option][hidden] {
    display: block !important;
    visibility: hidden;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: wp-coll-guard-reveal 0s 3s forwards;
  }

  @keyframes wp-coll-guard-reveal {
    to {
      visibility: visible;
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-aria-coll]').forEach(function (section) {
      if (!section.classList.contains('aria-coll--counting')) return;
      section.setAttribute('aria-busy', 'true');
      var cleared = false;
      function clear() {
        if (cleared) return;
        cleared = true;
        section.removeAttribute('aria-busy');
        observer.disconnect();
      }
      var observer = new MutationObserver(function () {
        if (!section.classList.contains('aria-coll--counting')) clear();
      });
      observer.observe(section, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['class'] });
      window.setTimeout(clear, 3200);
    });
  });
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection filter guard",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Collection filter guard"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
